# ast-grep

Shared rules for clone code that code checks. A convention that applies to several clones is written as a rule, not a paragraph in `AGENTS.md`: the agent can skip a paragraph, a check cannot be skipped.

The config is `../sgconfig.yml`. Run from the meta-repository root.

| Folder | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| [rules/](rules/README.md) | Rules, one file per rule |
| [rule-tests/](rule-tests/README.md) | Rule tests, one file per rule |

## Commands

```sh
ast-grep test --skip-snapshot-tests                 # rule tests
ast-grep scan --no-ignore parent repos/<name>       # one clone
mise run check                                      # everything together
```

The `--no-ignore parent` flag is needed because `repos/*` is in the meta-repository's `.gitignore`, and without the flag ast-grep skips the clones entirely. The clone's own `.gitignore`, for example `node_modules`, still applies.

## Current rules

There are no rules yet; the `code-rules` step of `mise run check` reports `no rules` and passes. The clones' own linters run in their `<name>:check` steps, and their rules are not duplicated here. A new rule is added with the `add-ast-grep-rule` skill.
